.TH "getIndex" "1" "" "SequoiaDB User Manuals" ""
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
getIndex \- get the specified index
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]db.collectionspace.collection.getIndex(<name>)\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
SdbCollection
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to get the specified index from current collection.
.SH PARAMETERS
.PP
name ( \f[I]string, required\f[] )
.PP
Index name, the length cannot exceed 127B, and cannot be an empty string, dot(.)
or dollar sign($).
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of type
BSONObj.
Users can get a list of collection details through this object.
For field descriptions, refer to SDB_SNAP_INDEXSTATS.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
The common exceptions of \f[C]getIndex()\f[] function are as follows:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
l l l l l.
T{
0
T}@T{
Error Code
T}@T{
Error Type
T}@T{
Description
T}@T{
Solution
T}
_
T{
1
T}@T{
\-47
T}@T{
SDB_IXM_NOTEXIST
T}@T{
Index doesn\[aq]t exist
T}@T{
Check if the index
T}
T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
T}@T{
exists
T}
.TE
.PP
When the exception happens, use [getLastErrMsg()][getLastErrMsg] to get the
error message or use getLastError() to get the error code.
For more details, refer to Troubleshooting.
.SH VERSION
.PP
v1.10 and above
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Get the index named ageIndex from the "sample.employee" collection.
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
>\ db.sample.employee.getIndex("ageIndex")
\f[]
.fi
.PP
The result is as follows:
.IP
.nf
